The **`classify`** function is defined in the *tool* namespace that was supplied by the developer.  
It isn’t part of the assistant’s internal code – it’s a “tool” that the system can invoke when you ask the assistant to run it.

Here’s where you’ll find it:

```text
namespace functions {
    type classify = (_: {
        acc_routing_start: string[],
    }) => any;
}
```

So, if you want to use it, you simply call the tool and pass an object with the `acc_routing_start` array of strings. The tool will then return whatever classification logic has been implemented behind it (the actual implementation is handled by the platform, not shown here).
